ci(windows): go back to --lib on the windows-tests job

--all was meant to cover the three binaries and the integration target, which
only ever built on Linux. On Windows under the windows-tests feature it fails
twice over, and the second failure has no cheap fix.

  error[E0425]: cannot find function `launch_windows_browser_host`
                in crate `cl_go_dash_lib`
  CVTRES : fatal error CVT1100: duplicate resource.
           type:MANIFEST, name:1, language:0x0409
  LINK   : fatal error LNK1123: failure during conversion to COFF

The first is the same shape as the cef_supervision defect fixed in 10437154:
lib.rs exports the function only when windows-tests is absent, main.rs calls it
whenever the target is Windows. Nothing is broken in production — that feature
exists for CI alone — but --all builds the binary and puts the two conditions
face to face.

The second is structural. build.rs embeds the test manifest through
cargo:rustc-link-arg, which reaches every linked target; the binaries already
carry a manifest of their own and the linker stops. Covering tests/ on Windows
means narrowing that injection to test targets (cargo:rustc-link-arg-tests),
which is its own piece of work. tests/ stays covered on Linux only.

The contract test moves with the job and now carries that reason. What it
protects is unchanged and still asserted: this job prepares no CEF, mounts no
CEF cache, and without native_browser no binary links libcef.dll.
